<!--
    GH-6930: function pointer argument rendered as 0x100000 (image base) instead of
    the function symbol.  https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/6930

    evhttp_write_cb has its entry at the rebased image base 0x100000.  It is passed as
    the writecb argument to the (undeclared) external bufferevent_setcb.  The sibling
    callback evhttp_error_cb (entry 0x105790) renders as a name, but the function at the
    base renders as the bare literal 0x100000.

    Root cause: ActionConstantPtr::isPointer (coreaction.cc) rejects the constant via the
    "bit_transitions(off,sz) less-than 3" bit-flag/mask heuristic.  0x100000 (one set bit,
    1 shifted left by 20) has a single bit transition, so the constant is never turned
    into a symbol reference and prints as the raw literal.  Stage model: S5 sub-stage
    const-pointer ("is this constant an address?"); the relaxation is exposed by a new
    P0 option (default off equals upstream behavior).

    Pass 1 (default pipeline) reproduces the bug: assert #1 is the bare 0x100000 literal
    as a call argument, while evhttp_error_cb DOES resolve.
    Pass 2 (after the fix toggle) would resolve 0x100000 to evhttp_write_cb. Placeholder
    until the option exists.
-->
